From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:56:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 112/117] misc: fastrpc: set the DMA mask before attaching the
 reserved memory

fastrpc_rpmsg_probe() attaches the channel's reserved memory region with
devm_of_reserved_mem_device_init() before it gives the rpmsg device a DMA
mask. The reserved memory core checks the region against the device's
mask and, with none set yet, warns at every boot that the reserved
memory is beyond the device's set DMA address range.

Set the 32-bit mask right after the channel context is allocated, before
the region is attached, and clear the device's dma_mask pointer again
when the probe fails and the context (which holds the mask) is freed.

Seen in the boot log of the OnePlus Pad 4 (Kaanapali); linux-next has the
same order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index a7050db966ee8..a55daefb8851e 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -2636,9 +2636,6 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (devm_of_reserved_mem_device_init(rdev))
-		dev_dbg(rdev, "no reserved DMA memory for FASTRPC\n");
-
 	vmcount = of_property_read_variable_u32_array(rdev->of_node,
 				"qcom,vmids", &vmids[0], 0, FASTRPC_MAX_VMIDS);
 	if (vmcount < 0)
@@ -2650,6 +2647,17 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 	if (!data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * Set the DMA mask before attaching the reserved memory region: the
+	 * region is checked against the mask, and without one the core warns
+	 * that the reserved memory is beyond the device's DMA address range.
+	 */
+	rdev->dma_mask = &data->dma_mask;
+	dma_set_mask_and_coherent(rdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+
+	if (devm_of_reserved_mem_device_init(rdev))
+		dev_dbg(rdev, "no reserved DMA memory for FASTRPC\n");
+
 	if (vmcount) {
 		data->vmcount = vmcount;
 		for (i = 0; i < data->vmcount; i++) {
@@ -2698,8 +2706,6 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 
 	atomic_set(&data->ctx_seq, 0);
 
-	rdev->dma_mask = &data->dma_mask;
-	dma_set_mask_and_coherent(rdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->users);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->invoke_interrupted_mmaps);
 	spin_lock_init(&data->lock);
@@ -2724,6 +2730,7 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 		misc_deregister(&data->secure_fdevice->miscdev);
 
 err_free_data:
+	rdev->dma_mask = NULL;
 	kfree(data);
 	return err;
 }
